course: dictionary
lesson: 10615
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Uneven can mean not flat, not equal, or not regular. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. «Fish can live with an uneven fin from birth or injury» means a fin that is not the same as the others.
explain: «Banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy, which means likely to pay back.» Then the text says «uneven income makes a bank more careful.» Income that comes in unevenly is not steady, so uneven means changing and not regular here. Always ask: what does the sentence need? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: On a safety sign, uneven ground means you might trip, so walk carefully. In a race, an uneven match has one side much stronger. Each time, the clues show which meaning you need.
fact: Uneven means not flat, smooth or level, as in an uneven path.
fact: Uneven can also mean not equal, as in uneven teams or an uneven share.
fact: Uneven can mean changing and not regular, as in uneven breathing.
fact: The opposite of uneven is even, which means flat, smooth or equal.
fact: In maths, odd is the usual word for numbers like 1, 3 and 5, so use odd there.
exercise: «Fish can live with an uneven fin from birth or injury and swim with their other fins and tail.» In this sentence, what does uneven mean? | Fast and strong | Smooth and flat | * Not the same as the others | Very quiet
exercise: «Uneven income makes a bank more careful.» What does uneven income suggest? | Income that never changes at all | Income that is paid in gold | Income that is very large | * Income that goes up and down, not steady
exercise: Which word is the opposite of uneven when we talk about a path? | Bumpy | Steep | Rocky | * Flat
test: Two children share 7 sweets. One gets 5 and the other gets 2. What kind of share is this? | Rounded | Fair | Even | * Uneven
test: Be careful, the ground is ___, so you might trip. Which word fits best? | Sweet | Light | * Uneven | Equal
exam: Ella's breathing became uneven when she was scared. What does uneven mean here? | * Changing and not regular | Equal to her friend's breathing | Flat, like a table | Smooth and calm
